---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_687",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 687,
  "text": "[[2947.7]] <b>522.  Joh. Lud. Praschii De lege caritatis commentatio ad Hug. Grotii opus de jure belli et pacis [Ende 1688 (?)]</b>\n [[2947.9]] <tab/>[Ende 1688 (?)] </p>\n<p> [[2947.15]] <b>Joh. Lud. Praschii</b> <i>De lege caritatis commentatio</i> <i>ad Hug. Grotii opus de jure\n[[2947.16]] belli et pacis.</i> </p>\n<p> [[2947.17]] [A2 r^#'o] Contra eos notat se scribere qui ex Christo faciunt alterum Draconem novas\n[[2947.18]] et severiores leges ferentem, in quo et peccaverit Grotius. Christus ipse non praeterire\n[[2947.19]] unum jota de lege; est enim perennis. </p>\n<p> [[2947.20]] [p. 7] Recte Rachelius praefatione <i>Otii Noviomagensis</i>: leges caritatis ne quidem\n[[2947.21]] quoad theoriam satis esse explicatas. </p>\n<p> [[2948.1]] [p. 10] Jus naturae corruptae est obteri innocentem posse qui fugae obstet, Grot.\n[[2948.2]] lib. 2. c. 1. n. 4. ut cum urgente necessitate alienum [licite] putatur rapi, lib. 2. c. 2 n. 6.\n[[2948.3]] Hujus juris summa: <i>proximus quisque est sibi.</i> Et de hoc intellige Epistolam Judae v. 10.\n[[2948.4]] Rom. I. v. 21, 32. Adde Calixti <i>Epit. Theol. mor.</i> c. <i>de leg.</i> p. 49. ad 61. Aliud est quod\n[[2948.5]] Deus quaedam constituit ex hypothesi naturae corruptae, ut circa bella judicia Paul.\n[[2948.6]] [1. Kor.] VI. v. 7. qui dicit et <greek>^%(/olvw ^%(/htthma</greek>. </p>\n<p> [[2948.7]] [p. 11] Dices Grotius scripsit non Christianis solis, sed humano generi. Respondeo,\n[[2948.8]] esto, oportebat tamen eos docere et sanare nec cum insanientibus furere. </p>\n<p> [[2948.9]] [p. 12] Caritas non differt a jure naturae. Distinguitur tamen caritas indefinite\n[[2948.10]] accepta a Christiana quae Christiano exhibenda, alia est liberalitas erga amplum jus\n[[2948.11]] ignotum, Petri 2. Epist. I. v. 7. <greek>filadelfía</greek> distincta ab <greek>ăgáphw</greek> et Paul. 1. Thess. 3.\n[[2948.12]] v. 12. </p>\n<p> [[2948.13]] [p. 13] Luthero <i>bruderliche liebe, gemeine liebe</i> inter omnes homines cognatio. </p>\n<p> [[2948.14]] [p. 14] Dilectio <greek>plh́rvma nómoy</greek> Paulo impletio legis Rom. XIII, v. 10. Add.\n[[2948.15]] vers. 8. et seq. </p>\n<p> [[2948.16]] [p. 14 sq.] Tullius in <i>officiis</i>: <i>omnes omnium <b>caritates</b> patria una complexa est</i>. </p>\n<p> [[2948.17]] [p. 16 sq.] Facessat sententia Socini, quod Christus autor legis perfectioris (+ licebit\n[[2948.18]] dicere Christum ob infirmitatem in aliis tolerata voluisse ad exactiorem normam revocare,\n[[2948.19]] ut polygamiam +). In doctrina Christi non agnoscimus distinctionem consilii a\n[[2948.20]] praecepto. Vide loca Matth. VII, v. 24, 1. Joh. III, vers. 21. 22, Jacob. IV. vers. 17.\n[[2948.21]] Schilterus <i>Jurispr. Christ.</i> cap. 10. Sed finge dari, an negligemus ut non data, an non\n[[2948.22]] tenebimur lege Gratitudinis. Plane qui id tantum quaerit quod salva conscientia sibi liceat,\n[[2948.23]] in eo <b>non videtur esse vera caritas</b>. Bonis haud sufficit Deum non offendere, sed\n[[2948.24]] ultro facere quod gratum esse sciunt. Qui debiles initio sunt oportet convalescere et ex\n[[2948.25]] pueris evadere viros. Seneca: <i>Latius patet officiorum quam juris regula.</i> Adde Grot.\n[[2948.26]] lib. 3. c. 10. Azor. <i>Inst. mor.</i> part. 2. lib. 12. c. 2. qu. 1, 6. </p>\n<p> [[2949.1]] [p. 18] Qui damnum dedit cujus reparatio potest exigi dicitur laesisse justitiam, qui\n[[2949.2]] secus caritatem, ita Grot. lib. 2. c. 17. n. 9. ubi ambigentes videas Zieglerum [et] Henniges\n[[2949.3]] in <i>Notis</i>. Actio caritatis dicitur quod non ex pacto etc. </p>\n<p> [[2949.4]] [p. 19] <i>Qui te angariaverit ad unum milliare, ito ad duo</i> ita Christus. Matth. V. 41.\n[[2949.5]] In secundo milliari est caritas. </p>\n<p> [[2949.6]] [p. 26 sq.] <i>Debemus animas pro fratribus ponere</i> 1. Joh. III, vers. 16. Balduinus\n[[2949.7]] debitum hoc de promtitudine explicat, et licere tantum putat <i>Cas. consc.</i> lib. 4, c. 17, v. 8,\n[[2949.8]] sed quid est promtitudo sine effectu. Adde Lactant. <i>Inst.</i> lib. 5. toto cap. 18. et Danhauer\n[[2949.9]] <i>Decal</i>. disp. 9. quaest. 2, 3. Negat Grot. hoc esse juris naturalis, lib. 1. c. 2. n. 6. Unde\n[[2949.10]] ergo innotuit Ethnicis. Vespasianus apud Suetonum c. 9. <i>periturum se potius quam\n[[2949.11]] perditurum</i>, adde Valer. Max. lib. 4, cap. 7. Si Damon Phintiasve alter alteri defuissent,\n[[2949.12]] violata erat amicitia, idem si quis dominum, conjugem, etc. in periculo deserit infamis.\n[[2949.13]] Cicero ait: probatum <i>quis bonus dubitet mortem oppetere, si sit ei profuturus</i>. Hoc\n[[2949.14]] Grotius quasi ex lege Christi. </p>\n<p> [[2949.15]] [p. 29] Scrupulus Grotii lib. 2, c. 25, n. 7. non teneri quem ad erumpiendum invasum\n[[2949.16]] si sine morte invasoris fieri non potest, nam <i>ex parte invasoris majus esse periculum\n[[2949.17]] damni sempiterni</i>. (+ Huic rationi Grotii non respondet. +)\n",
  "number": "522.",
  "title": "Joh. Lud. Praschii De lege caritatis commentatio ad Hug. Grotii opus de jure belli et pacis",
  "date": "[Ende 1688 (?)]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:522. Joh. Lud. Praschii De lege caritatis commentatio ad Hug. Grotii opus de jure belli et pacis [Ende 1688 (?)] [Ende 1688 (?)] Joh. Lud. Praschii De lege caritatis commentatio ad Hug. Grotii opus de jure belli et pacis. [A2 r^#'o] Contra eos notat se scribere qui ex Christo faciunt alterum Dracone...">
      <div class="text-content">
        {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
          paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>